WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.140
Borders is back and this time I went to Colombia.

00:00:07.560 --> 00:00:11.560
This country of about 50 million people actually feels like a lot of different countries,

00:00:11.680 --> 00:00:15.560
because the landscapes and the cultures are so different depending on where you go.

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:21.000
You can never cover all the stories in one
country,

00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:24.880
but I was able to assemble upon some of the most interesting things that I think are happening in Colombia.

00:00:25.460 --> 00:00:29.000
There is a crisis at this border and I went to go
see what's happening with the many

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:31.900
refugees that are coming from Venezuela
into Colombia

00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:33.320
and how Colombia is handling it.

00:00:35.140 --> 00:00:38.060
And then I went out into some of the
deepest jungle I'd ever been in

00:00:38.280 --> 00:00:44.100
to explore Colombia's cocaine economy, which
is based entirely on this one leaf:

00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:45.580
the coca plant.

00:00:47.560 --> 00:00:50.620
Oh and I got to see some
hippos during my trip, which was kind of weird.

00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:56.520
I also got to go up to the
beautiful city of Cartagena, up in the

00:00:56.520 --> 00:01:00.280
northern part of Colombia, to look into a
subject that I've never looked into before:

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:01.340
music and dance.

00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:10.040
So over the next few weeks, I'm going to start releasing these episodes,

00:01:10.040 --> 00:01:13.600
as always on Vox's YouTube
channel and on our Facebook Watch page

00:01:13.920 --> 00:01:15.960
I hope you like them, I hope you learn something new

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:19.600
and I hope you get to know Colombia on a whole new level.

